  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ready-Room Sortie Board, live",
    "overview": "The board is a squadron ready room's sortie board drawn inside BB, now covering the whole path a spec or work item travels: Open issues, Shaping, Ready, Flying, Landed. Each Flying spec has one ruled line with tickets in dependency order, small pixel chevrons between columns and a sky airstream behind the pegs. Work items have compact lane rows. The banner and lanes share the board's working-agent wind. What waits on the owner sits pinned near the top in amber. The path reads as a route, never as kanban columns or count tiles.\n\nThe material is BB's own theme. Ground, ink, muted ink and hairlines are BB's theme tokens, so the board works on any BB theme, light or dark. The only texture is ordered dither drawn on canvas: Bayer 8x8 thresholds, one cell per device pixel, so fills read as fine halftone grain. The only display type is a 5x7 pixel cell font for spec numbers, the banner stencil, section labels and path counts. Text sits on clean ground or flat tarmac. Four state inks sit on top of the theme, and each state is also carried by form, never by colour alone.\n\nMotion follows real work: the shared wind, working pegs, the Needs-you edge, each banner plane's lane state and observed takeoffs and landings. An observed queue-clearing landing earns one V fly-past. It pauses while the page is hidden. Under reduced motion every canvas draws one still frame and CSS motion stops.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "BB theme tokens for every neutral; four fixed state inks layered on top.",
      "Canvas Bayer 8x8 ordered dither at device-pixel density is the only texture. CSS adds none.",
